\newlabel{fig:metric_field}{{3}{4}{Metric tensor field for the 2-D Obstacles environment. (a)~The scalar field $g(x)$ inflates traversal cost near obstacles. (b)~Unit metric balls $\{v : v^\top G(x)\, v \le 1\}$: smaller balls near obstacles indicate higher traversal cost; larger balls in open space indicate cheaper movement.\relax }{figure.caption.3}{}}
