\newlabel{fig:sampling}{{4}{5}{Sampling strategies compared. (a)~Euclidean informed sampling draws uniformly from the prolate hyperspheroid $I_E$, wasting many samples in high-cost regions. (b)~Riemannian informed sampling draws from the tighter $I_R$, concentrating samples where they can improve the path.\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
